  "definition_ja": "値が変わらない、決まった数。a や k のような文字でも、1 つの決まった値を表すものは定数という。",
  "definition_en": "A quantity whose value does not change, such as 5 or −2. A letter like k is also a constant when it stands for one fixed number.",
  "latex": null,
  "spoken_en": null,
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "In y = kx, k is a constant; it stays the same while x and y change.",
      "ja": "y = kx の k は定数。x と y が変わっても、k は変わらない。",
      "register": "spoken"
    },
    {
      "en": "In y = ax + 3, a is a constant. If the graph passes through the point (2, 11), find the value of a.",
      "ja": "y = ax + 3 のグラフが点 (2, 11) を通るとき、定数 a の値を求めよ。",
      "register": "written"
    }
  ],
  "collocations": [],
  "pitfalls": [
    "比例定数は constant of proportionality、積分定数は constant of integration（エントリ constant-of-integration）。どちらも constant を使う。",
    "英語の constant は形容詞にもなり、「一定の」の意味で使う（a constant rate = 一定の割合、constant speed = 一定の速さ）。"
  ],
